# Banter in The Crimson Monastery (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is crimson_monastery): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ mon_ground_01_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:mon_ground and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Spiked black walls, red glass in every window, and the air smells like a butcher's tab gone sour. I'd say the house is marking the deck, friend.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at those courtyard statues, Silas, weeping fresh humours down the stonework without a single visible pump. The viscosity is a bit thin, though the sulfur masks it.
interject name:silas_vane: And hall doors with the spikes pointed inward, so you know the management really trusts the regulars. Let me get this bitter herb censer swinging before my ribs stain pink.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do leave me an unspoiled drop off the stone pulpit first, darling. I have never run an assay on masonry that bleeds on command.
interject name:silas_vane: Take a whole vial if you want, just don't ask me to double down on anything sitting in that Dead Larder.
endif
-> END

~ mon_upper_02_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:mon_upper and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: This balustrade over the courtyard is set square, Tobin, though the red glass ruins the light for proper ledger work. Too much glare on the docket.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Never mind the glass, Rook, smell those candles by the lecterns. That is not honest hive-wax, that is tallow rendered from fat, and it is smoking foul.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Aye, it leaves a greasy soot on the blank books and the masonry alike. Poor ventilation in the upper halls, and two chambers locked tight against inspection.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep two paces between me and those wicks while we pass the scriptorium. I would rather chew fifty-year ink than let a fat-spark catch in my collar.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Settle down now, I will walk on the candle side and keep the tower shield between the flame and your straw.
endif
-> END

~ mon_stables_03_lucan_delphine
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:delphine_ravelle and at:mon_stables and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Delphine, observe those boxes built into the dead trees beyond the yard. Bat hounds, if my nose has not lost its schooling in the horse-stink.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Charming accommodations, Lucan, though a crate of bloody treats is hardly top billing for the talent. Look at those little eyes opening in the bark like cheap seats.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Their kennel posture is terribly cramped, and I must deduct a full point for housing flying specimens above a prisoners' wagon. Barnaby is quite put out by the smell.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness just whispered a pun about barking up the wrong tree, and I am half tempted to throw him in the water trough.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Please restrain yourself, the warhorses are nervous enough with all this iron in the air.
endif
-> END

~ mon_bell_tower_04_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:mon_bell_tower and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Two floors of cold spiral stone and now a landing carpeted in fouled straw and gnawed bones. Mind the seams, darling, this staircase is a tragedy for velvet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My six eyes are dilating just looking at the bacterial culture in those dog beds, Delphine. One could harvest three distinct pathologies before reaching the twenty-foot ladder.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Keep your glass vials corked until we are through that trapdoor, because the stink of wet bat is already flattening my voice.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Notice the draft coming through the slit window over the valley. It keeps the air cool enough that the marrow in those bones has barely begun to sour.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: You have a crooked idea of a silver lining, Cordelia, now hold the rungs steady so I do not catch my hem.
endif
-> END

~ mon_sanctum_05_rook_silas
if name:rook_coldwake and name:silas_vane and at:mon_sanctum and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: A round altar on a stone island, and a moat of open blood with no grating or drainage slope. That is a slip hazard and a gross violation of parish decency.
interject name:silas_vane: Look at the stake they piled up, Rook, dried roses by the bushel and a chandelier burning like a high-roller's table. Tell's in the twitch, though, this whole room is a rig.
interject name:rook_coldwake: There is a journal left open on the stone and a painting of an elven woman set right beside the channel. No proper clerk leaves paperwork inches from an unsealed trough.
interject name:silas_vane: He painted her face like he was holding a winning hand and lost it on the turn of a single card.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the turf by the edge there, Silas, polished stone takes a slick film when the air is this damp.
endif
-> END

~ mon_cathedral_moon_06_cordelia_lucan
if name:cordelia_skein and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:mon_cathedral_moon and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: A fascinating sight in this dome, Lucan, how the blood moon pours through the red and violet glass like a stained slide. Even the spilled humours on the floor look calibrated.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, the dark has teeth under a roof like this, Cordelia, and the scent of old iron is pressing rather hard behind my eyes. Keep your voice steady, if you please.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your pulse is climbing past a hundred, though your diction remains admirably crisp. Shall I stand between you and the weeping statue while you take your notes?
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Thank you, yes, I would hate to let a feral snarl ruin my grading of the eastern altar's symmetry. Barnaby is already hiding behind my boots.
endif
-> END

~ mon_ground_07_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and at:mon_ground and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: The house lights are still wound-red, Rook, and the roses on the altar haven't wilted an inch, yet the whole octagon feels like a hall after the curtain drops.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The racket has gone out of the stonework, Delphine. My brass door-knocker hasn't given a single twitch since we came back through the courtyard.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Even the gate veteran looks like an usher waiting for someone to sweep up the programmes. I almost miss the tension, darling, it kept my stitching tight.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Quiet is good for the mortar, even when the walls have spikes on the wrong side. I ought to remember to draw a breath before we clear the gate.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Take two, Rook, and I will pluck a dry rose off the stone pulpit for my lining before we leave the cheap seats behind.
endif
-> END
